			"date": "2026-08-19T19:14:12.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> HTML-in-XML (RSS/Atom) is either 40% character entities by volume or malformed, and there’s always some RSS readers that can’t seem to guess right and decide the best method is to try neither</p><p>HTML-in JSON is 50% `\\?\\\"` by volume and we have yet to hit the adoption curve where somebody running a reader has an angry post about doing JSON Feed right, which concerns me</p>",
